{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-3038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡(1/x)}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-3038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡(1/x)}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{1}{x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\cdot (-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{tan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{x})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-3038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "328e24c13aae7c0da810d696d77a4c3b69fd38e4d9e9879538290a793255789e"} {"question" "q-3038" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-3038" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{1}{x})+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{1}{x})+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{x})+C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{x})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{1}{x})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-3038" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{x})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-10045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-10045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator, because\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nSo, let $u=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)$ | $1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)}^{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)}^{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-10045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "328e24c13aae7c0da810d696d77a4c3b69fd38e4d9e9879538290a793255789e"} {"question" "q-10045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-10045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2))-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2))"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2))-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2))"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-10045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-13474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int 4{x}^{2}{sec}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-13474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={x}^{3}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4{x}^{2}{sec}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int {sec}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int {sec}^{2}⁡(u)\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{3})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-13474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "328e24c13aae7c0da810d696d77a4c3b69fd38e4d9e9879538290a793255789e"} {"question" "q-13474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-13474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{3})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{3})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡({x}^{3})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{3})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{3})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-13474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{3})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-350060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}3{sec}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-350060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=x-\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi /4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\pi /4$ | $0$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}3{sec}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{0}{sec}^{2}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(u){|}_{-\\pi /4}^{0} \\\\  & =3(0-(-1)) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-350060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "328e24c13aae7c0da810d696d77a4c3b69fd38e4d9e9879538290a793255789e"} {"question" "q-350060" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-350060" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-350071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3}4\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-350071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=x-\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /3$ | $2\\pi /3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /6$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3}4\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}4\\operatorname{csc}⁡(u)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(u)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{csc}⁡(u){|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-4(\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =-4(1-2) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-350071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "328e24c13aae7c0da810d696d77a4c3b69fd38e4d9e9879538290a793255789e"} {"question" "q-350071" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" "file_sha256" "ca5bec1a2d194c88d5764feb7667ecebaa0533fe05085320e5ee14d0df4af2fb"} {"question" "q-350071" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030833/state.json" 